            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An expandable implant (22) for augmenting a vertebra including a vertebral body (VB) is presented. The expandable implant (22) comprises a distal end element (28) and a proximal end element (30) coaxially aligned with the distal end element (28), wherein each of the distal end element (28) and the proximal end element (30) are circular or oval so as to define an outer profile of the expandable implant (22) that is a cylinder or an oval prism. The expandable implant (22) further comprises a tissue support ski (26) comprising a tissue contact surface (54), a strut hub (32) secured to an underside of the tissue support ski (26) that is opposite the tissue contact surface (54), a distal strut (34) is secured to the strut hub (32), and further secured to the distal end element (28) at an angle so as to be angled towards the tissue support ski (26) in an undeployed configuration, and a proximal strut (36) is secured to the strut hub (32), and further secured to the proximal end element (30) at an angle so as to be angled towards the tissue support ski (26) in the undeployed configuration.</p>
            </abstract>
